| 522 | under walk, a strided range whose elements all fit raises `IntegerOverflow` at construction when a difference of its bounds leaves `ZZ32`: `MAX:MIN:1` (empty), `MIN:MAX:3` and `0:MIN:MIN` (two elements) raise | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | library bug (library) | `Specification/basic/expressions/ranges.tex`, "Ranges" | `ProjectFortress/tests/XXXStridedSpanWalk.fss` | climb batch 6.5b rung E and its skeptic | In `Library/RangeInternals.fss` at c124c6b65: `imposeStride` computes `dist = r-l` before it tests the stride's sign (`:1045-1055`, `:1048`); `ScalarRange.check()` computes `(l-r) MOD str` (`:195-202`, `:199`), which `fullScalarRange` (`:1713-1719`) reaches for every stride, 1 included; by reading, `StridedFullScalarRange.size`'s `right.get-left.get` (`:1458-1460`) overflows on a nonempty span beyond `ZZ32` whose size fits. Fix, without leaving `ZZ32` and keeping the checked operators (POSITIONS, "Fixed-width overflow raises `IntegerOverflow` under `walk`"): sign before distance; divisibility without `l-r`, stride `MIN` included; size split at zero. full text: history, row 522 |
